      "html": "<ul><li>Type: Stem plant</li><li>Origin: South America</li><li>Growth rate: Medium</li><li>Height: 3 - 10+ cm</li><li>Light demand: High</li><li>CO2: Medium</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Hydrocotyleverticillata(039)/4457",
      "html": "<p>Optimum growth is only achieved in strong light and soft, slightly acidic water. It does not need to be rooted, but can be used as a floating plant.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Hydrocotyleverticillata(039)/4457",
      "html": "<p>Unlike other Hydrocotyle species, this plant retains its trailing growth form. Verticillata originates from America and becomes 3-7 cm tall. Hydrocotyle verticillata is definitely a foreground plant, but also suitable for garden ponds. If the soil is kept moist, you may even use it as an indoor plant.</p>"
    }
  ],
